# CR 702.145c: any time a permanent is front face up with daybound and it is night, it transforms. Glasspool Mimic, a
# modal double-faced card (CR 712.3: one may transform), enters by day as a copy of Outland Liberator, so it has daybound;
# a copy effect on it does not stop it being represented by a double-faced card (CR 701.27a, 701.27c). When night comes,
# the Liberator becomes Frenzied Trapbreaker and the Mimic transforms too - back face up, yet still the copy of Outland
# Liberator its copy effect makes it (CR 707.2), so it keeps daybound and is not turned over again: back face up, it is
# no longer front face up with daybound.
#
# Turn 1: Forest and Mox Emerald cast Outland Liberator (it becomes day, CR 702.145d); Black Lotus casts Glasspool Mimic,
# copying it. Bot2 casts nothing on turn 2, so turn 3 is night (CR 731.2).

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Mox Emerald
Black Lotus
Outland Liberator
Glasspool Mimic
Island
Island
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Swamp x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Outland Liberator.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Hand.Glasspool Mimic.Cast
Bot1.Accept
[T1 Bot1.Main2]
? DayNight = Day
? Bot1.Battlefield.Outland Liberator#2.Transformed = (absent)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
DayNight = Night
Bot1.Battlefield = Forest; Frenzied Trapbreaker; Mox Emerald; Outland Liberator
Bot1.Battlefield.Frenzied Trapbreaker.Subtypes = Werewolf
Bot1.Battlefield.Outland Liberator.Subtypes = Human; Rogue; Shapeshifter; Werewolf
Bot1.Battlefield.Outland Liberator.Keywords = Daybound
Bot1.Battlefield.Outland Liberator.Transformed = true
